---
description: Synergy project brief, invariants, and parallel-agent rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read @AGENTS.md before writing code in this repo, and follow it.

It is the single shared brief for every agent regardless of editor: stack and commands,
where things live, invariants that fail silently when broken (Clerk token -> Supabase
RLS, per-request Supabase client, append-only migrations), known debt that is deferred
on purpose, and the rules for working alongside other agents in this tree.

Two that matter most when more than one agent is running:

- Do not fix build, type, or lint errors in files you did not edit. Wait 30 seconds and
  re-run — another agent is probably mid-edit.
- Never `git add -A` or `git commit -a`. Stage explicit paths only.

If AGENTS.md and anything else disagree, AGENTS.md wins. Keep it up to date: project
knowledge goes there, never into an editor-specific rules file.
